# UI quality floor

Before UI/UX/theme/layout/chart/copy work, read `docs/UI-GUARDRAILS.md`.

- Baseline: tag `ui-baseline-2026-11-07`, commit `83bcf8a`.
- Improve a named problem; avoid unsolicited global redesigns.
- Preserve Persian RTL, right rail, full-width desktop workspace, visual finance charts, local Vazirmatn, Lucide, mobile navigation, and three dark palettes.
- Keep cool green/blue/cyan accents. No decorative brown, beige, gold, or amber. Semantic warning/error colors are allowed.
- Use semantic CSS variables and shared components; no isolated hard-coded theme colors.
- Preserve stored theme/custom-color choices and all financial information shown.
- Before/after screenshots must use the same route and data at 375, 768, and 1440 px; check full-width pages at 1920 px.
- Block delivery on overflow, clipped content, weaker hierarchy, lost information, broken focus/keyboard behavior, poor contrast, or missing loading/empty/error states.
- Run frontend typecheck, tests, and production build after material changes.
- Document the reason, visual evidence, validation, and rollback commit.
